{"loc":"WAHIDI-WAJIZ:4:43-44","rows":[{"verses":["4:43"],"words":["لَا تَقْرَبُوا۟ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Prayer here means the places of prayer, namely mosques.","anchor":"أي: مواضع الصلاة، أي: المساجد","mentions":[]},{"verses":["4:43"],"words":["وَأَنتُمْ سُكَٰرَىٰ"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Before wine was finally prohibited, Muslims were forbidden to pray or enter a mosque while drunk and avoided intoxication at prayer times.","anchor":"نهوا عن الصلاة وعن دخول المسجد في حال السكر، وكان هذا قبل نزول تحريم الخمر","mentions":[]},{"verses":["4:43"],"words":["حَتَّىٰ تَعْلَمُوا۟ مَا تَقُولُونَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"A drunk person has a confused mind, babbles, and cannot sustain speech; if one knows what one says, one is not drunk and may pray and enter the mosque.","anchor":"والسكران المختلط العقل الذي يهذي، ولا يستمر كلامه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["4:43"],"words":["وَلَا جُنُبًا إِلَّا عَابِرِى سَبِيلٍ"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"A person in major ritual impurity must not approach the mosque except to pass through without staying.","anchor":"إلا إذا عبرتم المسجد فدخلتموه من غير إقامة فيه","mentions":[]},{"verses":["4:43"],"words":["حَتَّىٰ تَغْتَسِلُوا۟"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The restriction lasts until one performs the full ritual bath after major impurity.","anchor":"من الجنابة { وإن كنتم مرضى } أي: مرضا يضره الماء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["4:43"],"words":["وَإِن كُنتُم مَّرْضَىٰٓ"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"The relevant illness is one harmed by water, such as sores, smallpox, or wounds.","anchor":"أي: مرضا يضره الماء كالقروح، والجدري، والجراحات","mentions":[]},{"verses":["4:43"],"words":["أَوْ عَلَىٰ سَفَرٍ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"This means being on a journey.","anchor":"أي: مسافرين { أو جاء أحد منكم من الغائط }","mentions":[]},{"verses":["4:43"],"words":["أَوْ جَآءَ أَحَدٌۭ مِّنكُم مِّنَ ٱلْغَآئِطِ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Coming from al-ghāʾiṭ means having a bodily event.","anchor":"أو الحدث { أو لامستم النساء }","mentions":[]},{"verses":["4:43"],"words":["أَوْ لَٰمَسْتُمُ ٱلنِّسَآءَ"],"type":"meaning","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"Touching women means touching them with one’s hands.","anchor":"أي: لمستموهن بأيديكم فلم تجدوا ماء","mentions":[]},{"verses":["4:43"],"words":["فَلَمْ تَجِدُوا۟ مَآءًۭ فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟ صَعِيدًۭا طَيِّبًۭا"],"type":"law","speaker":"author","stance":"holds","claim":"When water is unavailable, perform dry ablution using clean earth that produces vegetation.","anchor":"تمسحوا بتراب طيب منبت","mentions":[]}]}
